CORE no-new-smt
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
memset with a symbolic size to a symbolic offset into an array of uint64_t,
and memset with a size of type uint8_t that is assumed to be 16, as
reported on #9187. Byte-operator lowering used to leave elements
unchanged.
With or without the fix, the new SMT back-end fails an invariant, hence
no-new-smt.
